<%#
  Goes beside the LABEL of a secret that is already stored: the same green tick
  the header nav uses for a module that is ready.

  It replaced `••••9876` in that position, and the reason is that the old
  version answered a question nobody was asking. Beside a label, the thing a
  developer wants to know is "is there a key in here" -- yes or no -- and four
  dots and a fragment of hex made them read a string to find out. The tick
  answers it at a glance and matches what the nav already taught them.

  The last four characters did not disappear; they moved into the box, as its
  placeholder, which is where "which key is in here" is actually asked. See
  _secret_field.

  "Set" rather than "Ready", deliberately. A stored key is present, not
  verified: nothing here has asked the provider whether it still works.
%>
<span class="ml-1.5 inline-flex align-middle">
  <%= render "sparrow_ui/console/status_glyph", ready: true, label: "Set" %>
  <span class="sr-only">Set</span>
</span>
